.TH QUORDON 1 "September 2026" "Quordon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quordon \- run the policy-enforcing infrastructure gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quordon
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quordon
provides local software agents with a strictly validated, policy-authorized,
read-only HTTP API for infrastructure services.
The current release supports MySQL 8.
.PP
The process refuses to start unless its policy is a regular file with mode
0600. Database credentials, query values, SQL, and raw driver errors are not
written to the audit stream.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fIPATH\fR, " " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Read the policy configuration from
.IR PATH .
The default is the value of
.B QUORDON_CONFIG
or
.BR config/policy.yaml .
.TP
.BR \-l " " \fIADDRESS\fR, " " \-\-listen " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Override the
.B server.listen
address from the policy configuration.
.B QUORDON_LISTEN
provides the same override when the command-line option is absent.
.TP
.BR \-v , " " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/quordon/policy.yaml
Default policy path used by the packaged systemd service.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/quordon/examples/policy.yaml
Non-operational example policy. Copy and edit it before enabling the service.
.SH SYSTEMD
The Debian package installs
.B quordon.service
but does not enable or start it automatically.
After installing a valid policy owned by the
.B quordon
user with mode 0600, run:
.PP
.EX
systemctl enable --now quordon.service
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://github.com/sigalx/quordon
